@baseUrl = http://localhost:8085

### Publish a global article: 202 Accepted, and a moment later ArticleService has stored it
# @name publish
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Scientists find a darn good way to clean the oceans",
  "content": "A new floating filter collects plastic without harming fish.",
  "author": "Christian",
  "region": "Global"
}

### The published article, read from ArticleService (through the load balancer). "darn" is masked.
GET http://localhost:8081/api/regions/global/articles/{{publish.response.body.$.id}}

### Publish to a continent: stored in that region's database
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Copenhagen opens its tenth harbour bath",
  "content": "Swimming in the city centre is free for everyone.",
  "author": "Christian",
  "region": "Europe"
}

### Unknown region gives 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Hello from nowhere",
  "content": "This region does not exist.",
  "author": "Christian",
  "region": "Atlantis"
}

# Trace demo: publish an article, then in Grafana (http://localhost:3000) open
# Drilldown -> Traces and pick "POST api/articles": ONE trace with PublisherService, ProfanityService,
# ArticleService and NewsletterService - the trace context crossed the ArticleQueue inside the message.
